  "root_causes": [
    "atom_fill_* IDs are enrich-injected development atoms; FanEdit v1.1 atomic catalog has no atom_fill IDs — cannot map without a separately agreed grounding protocol",
    "Many native event_* IDs also lack FH-…:E:event_* entries in pinned atomic_events.jsonl for this video (catalog size/IDs differ from delivery_out native IDs)",
    "EVENT_OUTSIDE_PREDICTED_WINDOW: even when an eval ID exists, predicted interval vs catalog event window fail overlap checks",
    "UNMAPPED_TAXONOMY: detector/8.31 subtypes such as throw_in_build_up_chain are absent from export CAUSAL_LABELS and/or FanEdit public causal taxonomy",
    "NO_EVAL_EVENT_IDS: after filtering unmapped/out-of-window, segment has empty eval event list — blocks strict export"
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Do not delete predictions or invent FanEdit IDs; keep native outputs + audit blockers",
    "Agree a common event-grounding protocol for atom_fill and native delivery IDs before changing the evaluator",
    "Add explicit reviewed_causal_mapping only for 8.31 types that have exact public FanEdit definitions — do not silent-relabel",
    "Separately reconcile delivery_out event_id namespace vs FanEdit FH-…:E:… catalog for FH-35DA83FD",
    "Window-overlap failures need prediction-interval convention review (raw t0_ms/t1_ms→sec already declared); not per-case stretching"
  ],
